The code attempts to securely execute `ls -l` on a user-provided directory and capture its output but has several flaws:

1. **Pipe Misconfiguration**: The child process incorrectly duplicates the read end of the pipe to stdout/stderr, preventing proper output capture. This leads to no data being read by the parent.

